  <h2>If the Sedgwick County Treasurer Has a Lien on Your House, I Can Help</h2>
  <p>If the Sedgwick County Treasurer's office has a delinquent tax lien on your property, or an IRS filing has shown up at the Register of Deeds, you've probably already discovered the problem: the title search catches it, the buyer's lender won't approve financing, and the deal dies before you ever reach closing. It happens constantly, and it's not a reflection of what kind of homeowner you are. Tax debt piles up fast when life gets hard — a job loss at Spirit AeroSystems, a medical crisis, a divorce that leaves you holding a house you can't afford on one income.</p>
  <p>I buy houses in Wichita with tax liens on them. Property tax liens, IRS liens, state tax liens, judgment liens — I've seen all of it. A lien doesn't mean you can't sell. It means you need a buyer who doesn't need a lender's blessing, and who knows how closing with a lien actually works in Kansas.</p>
  <p>That's exactly what I do. Call me at <strong>(316) 368-3344</strong> and we'll walk through your situation.</p>

